**Exact ordered word-level edit distance = 1,389 / 21,197 = 6.55% textual disagreement.** The Qwen file has **68 additional normalized words**; end **0.250 s earlier**. **This is not WER, measured accuracy, confirmed omissions or hallucination.**

**Normalization and computation:** extract all chronological SRT cue text; discard cue indexes/timecodes; strip `(speaker N)` labels; lowercase and remove ASCII/curly apostrophes joining contractions; replace other non-Unicode-letter/digit characters with whitespace, split on word boundaries; exact unit-cost Levenshtein (substitution, insertion, deletion each 1). Strip matching **95-token common prefix and 2-token suffix** to optimize without changing distance. Compute two-row dynamic programming within **±2,200-token diagonal band**. The optimal value **1,389** lies strictly within band; any path exiting would cost at least 2,200, establishing the **global exact** result. This is not a time-aligned candidate count. Complete P windows independently read to outro, complete Q parsed for metric, **selected Q passages interpreted independently**, not a full second narrative reading. No listening, MP3 clock calibration, source-audio input identity, speaker truth, run hyperparameters or human reference.

